Modifications include package-local APIs, explicit Hex8 data, geometry-only USD
metadata, sparse topology updates, and differentiable sparse time stepping.
The bear controller uses sparse FEM integration and checkpointed adjoints.

Research attribution: Breannan Smith, Fernando de Goes, Theodore Kim,
Stable Neo-Hookean Flesh Simulation, ACM TOG 37(2), article 12 (2018).
Cut topology uses the embedded affine-field construction of Eftychios Sifakis,
Kevin G. Der and Ronald Fedkiw, Arbitrary Cutting of Deformable Tetrahedralized
Objects, SCA (2007). See docs/method.md for implementation scope and paper links.
